SOH (sin): Sine equals the oppostie side length divided by the hypotenuse length (sin = Opposite/Hypotenuse)

CAH (cos): Cosine equals the adjacent side lenth divied by the hypotenuse lenth(cos = Adjacent/Hypotenuse)

TOA (tan): Tagnent equals the opposite side lenth divied by the adjacent side lenth (tan = Opposite/Adjacent)


Cosencant = Hypotenuse/Opposite


Secant = hypotenuse/adjacent

Cotangent = adjacent/opposite
